// Focused view: Delivery service with its direct neighbors only.

views {
  style element.tag = #frontend   { color blue }
  style element.tag = #backend    { color sky }
  style element.tag = #data       { color secondary }
  style element.tag = #adminPlane { color indigo }
  style element.tag = #federation { color green }

  view serviceDelivery of velox.deliveryService {
    title "Services / Delivery"
    description '''
      Realtime hub over bidirectional WebTransport (QUIC). Sequences MLS commits via
      Valkey epoch leases, then publishes to Kafka for fan-out.

      ---

      **WebTransport** — Bidirectional QUIC protocol. Clients send commits and receive
      pushes over the same persistent connection with independent per-stream flow control.

      **Epoch Lease** — Short-lived lock (`{epoch: N, holder: clientId, expires: TTL}`)
      stored in Valkey. Delivery issues it before a commit and advances the epoch on success.

      **CAS (Compare-And-Swap)** — Atomic Valkey operation used to enforce epoch ordering.
      Only one client can hold the lease at a time; the epoch only advances if the stored
      value matches, preventing two clients from committing at the same epoch.

      **Ratchet Tree** — MLS internal data structure tracking group membership. Delivery
      hot-caches the current ratchet tree in Valkey so lease holders can validate commits
      without a round-trip to Scylla.

      **user-state** — Umbrella Kafka topic + Valkey namespace for ephemeral per-user
      signals: presence (online/offline), typing indicators, read receipts, and future
      ephemeral props. Tracked in Delivery Valkey and fanned out via Kafka.

      **Client-side commit construction** — The client (not Delivery) encrypts and
      constructs every MLS Commit. Delivery only validates the epoch lease and forwards —
      it never sees plaintext or private key material.
    '''
    include *
    include -> velox.deliveryService ->
    autoLayout LeftRight 120 80
  }
}
